128
00:14:15,856 --> 00:14:24,096
These are your criminal hackers who try to profit from their crimes and they will have a malicious intent in trying to hack a victim organization.

129
00:14:24,256 --> 00:14:28,336
The grey hats are individuals who work both offensively and defensively.

130
00:14:28,416 --> 00:14:29,216
What does that mean?

131
00:14:29,390 --> 00:14:44,336
They could work as black hat hackers with malicious intent and try to harm some organization, while on the other hand, they would also try to work as a security analyst and try to enhance the security posture of an organization for a remuneration.

132
00:14:44,654 --> 00:14:49,936
Third one, which is white hat, which is what we want to be or what we want to achieve ourselves as.

133
00:14:50,096 --> 00:14:58,256
An individual who professes the same skills as a black hat hacker, probably uses the same tools, has the same kind of knowledge, but the intent is different.

134
00:14:58,336 --> 00:15:15,456
They're going to use them for defensive purposes, there's no malicious intent, they act with authorization from the organization, and they will try to detect any flaws and try to plug out those flaws so that black hat hackers would not be able to misuse those flaws to gain access.

135
00:15:15,726 --> 00:15:16,708
Suicide hackers.

136
00:15:16,896 --> 00:15:24,176
Now, individuals who aim to bring down critical infrastructure for a cause and are not worried about facing jail terms or any other punishment.

137
00:15:24,336 --> 00:15:42,016
So, any people or any organization or a group of people, for example, anonymous or these kind of organized hackers, they have a political cause or a social cause that they want to promote and they do this by hacking critical infrastructure of organizations, bringing it down, defacing their website.

138
00:15:42,176 --> 00:15:45,376
Now, why would these not be classified as black hat hackers?

139
00:15:45,536 --> 00:15:50,816
The main difference between black hat hackers and suicide hackers is that black hat hackers will try to hide their identity.

140
00:15:50,990 --> 00:16:00,576
They will always have a fake identity that they will utilize and try to hide behind it, whereas suicide hackers will claim responsibility for the attacks that they have done and will boast about it.

141
00:16:00,736 --> 00:16:04,656
They will not be worried about facing repercussions for the attacks that they have done.

142
00:16:04,942 --> 00:16:05,712
The script kiddie.

143
00:16:05,806 --> 00:16:13,392
A script kiddie is an unskilled hacker who compromises systems by running scripts, tools and softwares already developed and already made available by real hackers.

144
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:18,032
So these guys have very minimal technical knowledge, they have no idea how that attack works.

145
00:16:18,286 --> 00:16:22,752
They're just going to use an automated tool, click on a few buttons and hope that the attack succeeds.

146
00:16:22,912 --> 00:16:23,952
A cyber terrorist.

147
00:16:24,192 --> 00:16:32,192
Individuals with wide range of skills motivated by religious or political beliefs to create fear by large scale disruption of computer networks.

148
00:16:32,352 --> 00:16:49,072
We could talk about organizations like ISIS who have a lot of digital propaganda that they use and target weak-minded people to join their causes, or people who spread ransomware who terrorize organizations and hold them to ransom and demand money from them by encrypting their data.

149
00:16:49,326 --> 00:16:50,512
