150
00:16:50,672 --> 00:16:56,752
Individuals employed by the government to penetrate and gain top secret information and to damage information systems to other governments.

151
00:16:56,992 --> 00:17:00,912
The best example would be the cyber wars that are going on these days.

152
00:17:01,312 --> 00:17:14,192
Most of the organizations, most of the countries nowadays would have a secret cyber cell consisting of highly skilled hackers who are interested with the task of spying on the enemies and trying to gather information by hacking into their infrastructure.

153
00:17:14,352 --> 00:17:20,672
Now it is not going to be a legit job, it will always be masked by a legit organization, but this does happen.

154
00:17:20,846 --> 00:17:21,551
Hacktivism.

155
00:17:21,712 --> 00:17:26,031
Individuals who promote a political agenda by hacking, especially defacing or disabling websites.

156
00:17:26,432 --> 00:17:32,672
the difference between suicide hackers and hacktivism is suicide hackers have a social cause that they want to promote.

157
00:17:32,832 --> 00:17:40,100
Hacktivists would have a political agenda and they are going to deface websites and they're going to promote their agenda by defacing such websites.

158
00:17:40,366 --> 00:17:43,632
Alright, so let's talk about some common attacks in cybersecurity.

159
00:17:43,872 --> 00:17:48,112
The most common attack ever seen in today's world is a denial of service attack.

160
00:17:48,272 --> 00:18:00,112
So this is where the hacker tries to consume the resources of the victim server in such a way that there are no resources available for legitimate users to connect to the server and conduct their business.

161
00:18:00,366 --> 00:18:12,912
Other attacks that you will face would be malware attacks where there would be a malicious software that would deliver a Trojan virus or a worm to the victim, thus infecting the victim's machine and rendering it useless.

162
00:18:13,230 --> 00:18:26,832
A man in the middle attack where the hacker would put himself in between your machine and the router and start sniffing data packets that you're sending, thus trying to compromise information contained within those packets.

163
00:18:27,054 --> 00:18:45,072
So the phishing attack is where a hacker will send a seemingly legitimate looking message to you, an email, let's say, asking you to perform certain actions where the hacker would be impersonating another organization and you fall prey to that and end up giving your confidential information.

164
00:18:45,390 --> 00:18:56,752
A drive-by attack, cross-site scripting attacks where web applications get compromised and scripts are embedded within those applications or within commands that are sent out by the users.

165
00:18:56,992 --> 00:19:07,472
Password attacks where your hackers try to compromise the passwords of users by cracking them based either on brute force, dictionary-based attacks, or password guessing.

166
00:19:07,726 --> 00:19:23,552
Eavesdropping attacks, this could be physical in nature, where somebody overhears what you're saying or tries to capture data packets that contain your VoIP transmissions where let's say you're assuming you're making a Skype or a link-based call.

167
00:19:23,790 --> 00:19:32,592
SQL injection attacks where again attackers will target your database, try to send in malicious queries which will compromise your database and the data within.

168
00:19:32,752 --> 00:19:48,752
But the attacks it is based on cryptography, uh, where there are uh where you're looking at permutations on combinations of how algorithm functions, and then you're looking at the permutations on how many times the processing needs to be done for that algorithm to be reversed.

169
00:19:48,912 --> 00:19:51,792
So these are some of the most common attacks in cybersecurity.

