03:39:41,632 --> 03:39:54,272
With the extensive use of the internet and modern technologies, there is a massive challenge in protecting all our digital data, such as net banking information, account credentials, and medical reports, to name a few.

2606
03:39:54,512 --> 03:39:57,792
Have you heard about the deadly WannaCry ransomware attack?

2607
03:39:58,032 --> 03:40:03,472
The attack happened in May 2017 in Asia, and then it spread across the world.

2608
03:40:03,712 --> 03:40:10,112
Within a day, more than 230,000 computers were infected across 150 countries.

2609
03:40:10,352 --> 03:40:15,232
The WannaCry CryptoWorm encrypted the data and locked the users out of their systems.

2610
03:40:15,472 --> 03:40:21,712
For decryption of the data, the users were asked for a ransom of $300 to $600 in Bitcoin.

2611
03:40:21,952 --> 03:40:31,792
The users who used the unsupported version of Microsoft Windows and those who hadn't installed the security update of April 2017 were targeted in this attack.

2612
03:40:32,032 --> 03:40:34,992
The WannaCry attack took a toll on every sector.

2613
03:40:35,232 --> 03:40:43,552
Top-tier organizations like Hitachi, Nissan, and FedEx had to put their businesses on hold as their systems were affected too.

2614
03:40:43,872 --> 03:40:46,912
Now, this is what you call a cyber attack.

2615
03:40:47,152 --> 03:40:50,432
To prevent such attacks, cybersecurity is implemented.

2616
03:40:50,672 --> 03:40:59,552
We can define cybersecurity as the practice of protecting networks, programs, computer systems, and their components from unauthorized digital attacks.

2617
03:40:59,712 --> 03:41:02,832
These illegal attacks are often referred to as hacking.

2618
03:41:03,232 --> 03:41:06,352
Hacking refers to exploiting weaknesses in a computer network.

2619
03:41:06,672 --> 03:41:09,312
To obtain unauthorized access to information.

2620
03:41:09,552 --> 03:41:13,392
A hacker is a person who tries to hack into computer systems.

2621
03:41:13,632 --> 03:41:16,912
This is a misconception that hacking is always wrong.

2622
03:41:17,072 --> 03:41:19,792
There are hackers who work with different motives.

2623
03:41:20,032 --> 03:41:22,672
Let's have a look at three different types of hackers.

2624
03:41:22,912 --> 03:41:28,112
Black hat hackers are individuals who illegally hack into a system for monetary gain.

2625
03:41:28,272 --> 03:41:37,232
On the contrary, we have white hat hackers who exploit the vulnerabilities in a system by hacking into it with permission in order to defend the organization.

2626
03:41:37,392 --> 03:41:40,752
This form of hacking is absolutely legal and ethical.

2627
03:41:40,912 --> 03:41:44,192
Hence, they are also often referred to as ethical hackers.

2628
03:41:44,432 --> 03:41:48,192
In addition to these hackers, we also have the gray hat hackers.

2629
03:41:48,352 --> 03:41:52,832
As the name suggests, the color gray is a blend of both white and black.

2630
03:41:52,992 --> 03:41:59,872
These hackers discover vulnerabilities in a system and report it to the system's owner, which is a good act.

2631
03:42:00,192 --> 03:42:03,312
But they do this without seeking the owner's approval.

2632
03:42:03,552 --> 03:42:09,312
Sometimes gray hat hackers also ask for money in return for the spotted vulnerabilities.

2633
03:42:09,552 --> 03:42:18,752
Now that you have seen the different types of hackers, let's understand more about the hacking that is legal and valid, ethical hacking, through an interesting story.

