Nmap uses raw IP packets in novel ways to determine what hosts are available on the network, what services these hosts are offering, what operating systems they are running and their versions, what type of packet filters and firewalls are in use, and dozens of other characteristics.

3764
05:44:16,814 --> 05:44:21,924
It was designed to rapidly scan large networks but works fine against single hosts as well.

3765
05:44:23,438 --> 05:44:36,068
Since every application that connects to a network needs to do so via a port, the wrong port or server configuration can open a can of worms which lead to a thorough breach of the system and ultimately a fully hacked device.

3766
05:44:38,190 --> 05:44:40,292
Next on the list we have Metasploit.

3767
05:44:42,510 --> 05:44:51,748
The Metasploit framework is a very powerful tool that can be used by cybercriminals as well as ethical hackers to probe systemic vulnerabilities on networks and servers.

3768
05:44:52,174 --> 05:45:00,484
As a part of the third stage of penetration testing, it's an open source framework which can be easily customized and used with most operating systems.

3769
05:45:01,934 --> 05:45:10,020
With Metasploit, the ethical hacking team can use a ready-made or custom code and introduce it into a network to probe for weak spots.

3770
05:45:10,592 --> 05:45:20,260
As another flavor of threat hunting, once these flaws are identified and documented, the information can be used to address systemic weaknesses and prioritize solutions.

3771
05:45:22,638 --> 05:45:29,764
Once a particular vulnerability is identified and the exploit is fed into the system, there are a host of options for the hacker.

3772
05:45:30,382 --> 05:45:41,732
Depending on the vulnerability, hackers can even run root commands from the terminal, allowing complete control over the activities of the compromised system as well as all personal data stored on the device.

3773
05:45:44,142 --> 05:45:53,860
A big advantage of Metasploit is the ability to run full-fledged scans on a target system, thereby giving a detailed picture of the security index of said system.

3774
05:45:55,502 --> 05:46:01,252
This also provides the necessary exploits that can be used to bypass the firewalls and the antivirus software.

3775
05:46:01,472 --> 05:46:11,268
Having a single solution to gather almost all the necessary points of attack is very useful for ethical hackers and penetration testers as denoted by the high rank in this list.

3776
05:46:14,670 --> 05:46:16,612
At number 3 we have Wireshark.

3777
05:46:17,632 --> 05:46:22,628
Wireshark is the world's foremost and widely used networking protocol analyzer.

3778
05:46:23,086 --> 05:46:33,924
It lets you see what's happening on your network at a microscopic level and is a de facto standard across many commercial and non-profit enterprises, government agencies and educational institutions.

3779
05:46:35,054 --> 05:46:41,380
Wireshark is a popular open source tool to capture network packets and converts them to human readable binary format.

3780
05:46:41,646 --> 05:46:45,604
It provides every single detail of the organization's network infrastructure.

3781
05:46:46,254 --> 05:46:50,468
It consists of devices designed to help measure the ins and outs of the network.

3782
05:46:51,150 --> 05:47:04,452
The information collected through Wireshark can be used for various purposes such as real-time or offline network analysis, identification of the traffic coming onto your network, its frequency and its latency between specific hops.

3783
05:47:05,038 --> 05:47:09,312
This helps network administrators generate statistics based on real-time data.

3784
05:47:10,638 --> 05:47:21,952
Wireshark is also a cross-platform tool that can be installed on Windows, Linux, and Mac systems to enable hackers and all ecosystems to monitor network traffic irrespective of the operating system.

3785
05:47:22,881 --> 05:47:28,432
The Development team is determined to maintain this level of freedom for their users in the foreseeable future.

3786
05:47:32,014 --> 05:47:36,964
The next tool on our list is AirGarden, which is a part of the third phase of penetration testing.

3787
05:47:38,318 --> 05:47:46,724
This is a multi-use bash script for Linux systems to hack and audit wireless networks like our everyday Wi-Fi router and its counterparts.

3788
05:47:47,598 --> 05:48:07,588
Along with being able to launch denial of service attacks on compromised networks, this multipurpose Wi-Fi hacking tool has very rich features which support multiple methods for Wi-Fi hacking, including Multified WPS, hacking modes, all-in-one WEP attack, handshake file capturing, evil twin attacks, pixie dust, and so much more.

3789
05:48:08,526 --> 05:48:17,316
It usually needs an external network adapter that supports monitor mode, which is necessary to be able to capture wireless traffic traversing the air channels.

3790
05:48:19,118 --> 05:48:32,612
Thanks to its open source nature, AirGarden can be used with multiple community plugins and add-ons, thereby increasing its effectiveness against a wide variety of routers, both in the 2.4 GHz band and 5 GHz band.

3791
05:48:34,222 --> 05:48:36,132
The next tool is John the Ripper.

3792
05:48:37,006 --> 05:48:44,068
John the Ripper is an open source password security auditing and password recovery tool available for many operating systems.

3793
05:48:45,006 --> 05:49:00,868
JohnTheRipper Jumbo supports hundreds of hash and cipher types, including for use of passwords of operating systems, web apps, groupware, database servers, network traffic captures, encrypted private keys, file systems and document files.

3794
05:49:01,294 --> 05:49:17,796
Some of the key features of the tool include offering multiple modes to speed up password tracking, automatically detecting the hashing algorithm used by the passwords, and the ease of running and configuring the tool, making it a password tracking script of choice for novices and professionals alike.

3795
05:49:19,182 --> 05:49:27,716
It can use dictionary attacks along with regular brute forcing to speed up the process of cracking the correct password without wasting additional resources.

3796
05:49:28,686 --> 05:49:35,844
The word list being used in this dictionary attacks can be used from the user's end, allowing for a completely customizable process.

