07:11:08,014 --> 07:11:14,564
Today we will see the starting journey in cybersecurity that is super exciting but can be a bit daunting.

4539
07:11:14,958 --> 07:11:21,796
So to help you out, we are going to talk about some common mistakes that beginners often make and how you can avoid them.

4540
07:11:22,254 --> 07:11:27,588
If you're just getting started or looking to improve your skills, this guide will set you on the right path.

4541
07:11:27,854 --> 07:11:33,024
So let's dive in and make sure your cybersecurity career gets off to a strong start.

4542
07:11:33,184 --> 07:11:38,544
So let's get started and we'll see the worst beginner cybersecurity mistakes everyone makes.

4543
07:11:38,798 --> 07:11:42,116
And we'll start with the number one point that is ignoring basics.

4544
07:11:42,542 --> 07:11:50,052
So many beginners rush into advanced topics without mastering the basics, which can lead to confusion and frustration later on.

4545
07:11:50,224 --> 07:11:54,244
It's essential to build a strong foundation before diving into complex subjects.

4546
07:11:54,704 --> 07:11:57,572
If we talk about number one is understanding networking.

4547
07:11:58,190 --> 07:12:00,544
Networking is the backbone of cybersecurity.

4548
07:12:00,782 --> 07:12:07,556
Learn how data travels across networks, different types of networks like LAN and WAN, and basic networking protocols.

4549
07:12:08,014 --> 07:12:14,404
Knowing how network protocol functions help you understand how attacks occur and how to defend against them.

4550
07:12:14,926 --> 07:12:17,264
Then comes mastering operating systems.

4551
07:12:17,646 --> 07:12:22,948
So operating systems are another critical area, whether it's Windows, Linux, or Mac OS.

4552
07:12:23,344 --> 07:12:30,704
You need to know how different OS work and learn about file systems, user management, and basic command line skills.

4553
07:12:30,864 --> 07:12:35,428
So this knowledge is crucial for tasks like malware analysis and system hardening.

4554
07:12:35,918 --> 07:12:37,744
Then comes the basic coding skills.

4555
07:12:37,870 --> 07:12:40,708
So coding is an invaluable skill in cybersecurity.

4556
07:12:41,006 --> 07:12:49,584
You can start with a simple language like Python and learn how to write scripts to automate tasks, analyze data, and understand the logic behind software vulnerabilities.

4557
07:12:49,744 --> 07:12:56,548
So basic coding skills will help you comprehend how attacks are carried out and how to develop countermeasures.

4558
07:12:57,006 --> 07:13:05,184
So taking the time to master these basics will make advanced topics much easier to understand and will set a solid foundation for your career in cybersecurity.

4559
07:13:05,390 --> 07:13:11,024
So remember, it's a journey and starting with the basics will ensure you build strong, lasting knowledge.

4560
07:13:11,264 --> 07:13:15,812
Now we'll come to number second point that is skipping hands-on practice.

4561
07:13:16,174 --> 07:13:19,876
So this is also one of the cybersecurity mistakes that beginners make.

4562
07:13:20,304 --> 07:13:30,084
Cybersecurity isn't just about theory, practical experience is crucial, and many beginners focus too much on reading and studying without applying what they have learned.

4563
07:13:30,574 --> 07:13:33,412
This creates a gap between knowledge and real world skills.

4564
07:13:33,806 --> 07:13:36,464
So the number one point here is setting up a home lab.

4565
07:13:36,784 --> 07:13:47,492
So create a home lab with an old computer or virtual machine to practice what you learn, install different operating systems, set up networks, and simulate attacks in a controlled environment.

4566
07:13:47,726 --> 07:13:49,444
Then comes real world scenarios.

4567
07:13:49,742 --> 07:13:55,824
So use your home lab to practice real-world scenarios like configuring firewalls and detecting intrusions.

4568
07:13:56,142 --> 07:14:02,980
Platforms like Hack the Box and Try Hack Me offer cybersecurity challenges that mimic real life networks and systems.

4569
07:14:03,374 --> 07:14:04,864
Then comes building confidence.

4570
07:14:05,134 --> 07:14:07,140
So hands-on practice builds confidence.

4571
07:14:07,342 --> 07:14:14,404
So solving real problems and seeing the results of your actions make you more comfortable with cybersecurity tools and techniques.

4572
07:14:14,798 --> 07:14:19,184
And this confidence is crucial when making quick, informed decision in this field.

4573
07:14:19,374 --> 07:14:27,876
So gaining practical experience bridges the gap between theory and practice, making you a more effective and confident cybersecurity professional.

4574
07:14:28,078 --> 07:14:34,464
So now we'll see the third mistake that cybersecurity beginners make that is lack of documentation.

4575
07:14:34,958 --> 07:14:40,292
So, documenting your work is a crucial yet often overlooked aspect of cybersecurity.

4576
07:14:40,590 --> 07:14:47,396
Many beginners focus solely on learning new skills and solving problems without keeping track of their progress.

4577
07:14:47,630 --> 07:14:52,868
However, good documentation practices can significantly enhance your learning experience.

4578
07:14:53,102 --> 07:15:01,264
And by keeping detailed notes on what you learn, the tools you use, and the methods you apply, you create a valuable resource for future reference.

4579
07:15:01,422 --> 07:15:06,948
And this habit helps you review and reinforce your knowledge, making it easier to remember complex concepts.

4580
07:15:07,278 --> 07:15:15,940
Additionally, well-documented work allows you to share your insights and solutions with others, whether through blogs, presentations, or team collaborations.

4581
07:15:16,238 --> 07:15:22,116
It also helps in troubleshooting as you can quickly revisit your steps to identify where something might have gone wrong.

4582
07:15:22,304 --> 07:15:28,704
So in the professional world, documentation is essential for maintaining clear and efficient communication within a team.

4583
07:15:28,814 --> 07:15:34,624
And by starting this practice early, you will develop a habit that will benefit you throughout your career.

4584
07:15:34,958 --> 07:15:42,304
And now we'll move to the fourth cybersecurity mistake for beginners that is waiting too long to start applying for jobs.

4585
07:15:42,544 --> 07:15:49,764
So a common mistake many beginners make is waiting until they feel perfectly qualified before applying for cybersecurity jobs.

4586
07:15:50,350 --> 07:15:52,612
This approach can be counterproductive.

4587
07:15:52,910 --> 07:16:01,028
The truth is you might never feel completely ready, and waiting too long can cause you to miss out on a valuable opportunity.

4588
07:16:01,454 --> 07:16:04,064
So start applying for jobs early in your learning journey.

4589
07:16:04,224 --> 07:16:08,164
The process of applying and interviewing is a learning experience in itself.

4590
07:16:08,462 --> 07:16:13,984
It helps you understand what employers are looking for and it can highlight areas where you need to improve.

4591
07:16:14,094 --> 07:16:19,940
So early job applications also provide you with real-world feedback and networking opportunities.

4592
07:16:20,238 --> 07:16:25,732
Remember, many entry-level positions are designed for people who are still learning and growing in this field.

4593
07:16:25,934 --> 07:16:33,732
So employers often value enthusiasm, willingness to learn, and problem solving skills as much as they do technical knowledge.

4594
07:16:34,094 --> 07:16:37,540
So by starting early, you can gain experience and build confidence.

4595
07:16:37,998 --> 07:16:40,708
Even if you are not yet perfectly qualified.

4596
07:16:41,070 --> 07:16:45,104
And then comes the next mistake that is trying to qualify for all jobs.

4597
07:16:45,358 --> 07:16:51,664
So in the vast field of cybersecurity, trying to qualify for every job out, there is a common but misguided approach.

4598
07:16:51,918 --> 07:16:59,588
Cybersecurity encompasses a wide range of specialities from network security and ethical hacking to incident response and security analysis.

4599
07:16:59,982 --> 07:17:07,108
Instead of spreading yourself thin trying to learn everything, focus on a key few areas and become proficient in them.

4600
07:17:07,534 --> 07:17:11,620
Specializing in special fields make you more valuable to potential employers.

4601
07:17:11,982 --> 07:17:16,676
It's better to be an expert in one or two areas than to have superficial knowledge in many.

4602
07:17:16,814 --> 07:17:23,716
So by focusing on specific skills, you can develop a better understanding and expertise that sets you apart from others.

4603
07:17:23,982 --> 07:17:31,344
So this focused approach also makes it easier to stay updated with the latest trends and advancements in your chosen areas.

4604
07:17:31,504 --> 07:17:38,564
Remember, depth of knowledge often outweighs breadth when it comes to career advancement and job satisfaction.

4605
07:17:39,438 --> 07:17:42,404
So this was all about trying to qualify for all jobs.

4606
07:17:42,734 --> 07:17:46,544
Now we'll see the biggest mistake that is IT foundation fallacy.

4607
07:17:46,798 --> 07:17:51,744
So many aspiring cybersecurity professionals believe they need a deep IT background to start their career.

4608
07:17:51,904 --> 07:17:55,664
This is same as the number one point, but this is a misconception.

4609
07:17:56,078 --> 07:18:01,984
While having a solid foundation in IT can be beneficial, it's not a prerequisite for success in cybersecurity.

4610
07:18:02,144 --> 07:18:05,668
What you need are the specific skills and practical experience.

4611
07:18:06,094 --> 07:18:09,904
Focus on learning about networks, operating systems, and security tools.

4612
07:18:10,094 --> 07:18:14,340
Engage in hands-on practice through labs and simulations to build real-world skills.

4613
07:18:14,704 --> 07:18:21,664
Cybersecurity is a field where practical knowledge and the ability to apply concepts matter more than theoretical IT knowledge.

4614
07:18:21,824 --> 07:18:27,824
And many successful cybersecurity professionals come from diverse backgrounds, including those with minimal IT experience.

4615
07:18:28,046 --> 07:18:31,908
So they succeed by continuing learning and adapting to new challenges.

4616
07:18:32,398 --> 07:18:35,652
So don't let the lack of deep IT foundation hold you back.

4617
07:18:35,854 --> 07:18:42,180
Concentrate on gaining the skills and experience that are directly relevant to the cybersecurity roles you are interested in.

4618
07:18:42,702 --> 07:18:46,244
Now moving to number 7, that is not attending cybersecurity events.

4619
07:18:46,480 --> 07:18:51,652
So attending cybersecurity events is one of the best ways to stay updated and connected in the field.

4620
07:18:51,840 --> 07:19:01,040
These events, including conferences, webinars, and meetups, offer a wealth of information on the latest trends, tools, and threats in cybersecurity.

4621
07:19:01,134 --> 07:19:07,600
They provide a platform to learn from experts, gain insights into industry developments, and discover new technologies.

4622
07:19:07,840 --> 07:19:11,108
Additionally, these events are excellent networking opportunities.

4623
07:19:11,534 --> 07:19:16,640
Meeting other professionals that can lead to job opportunities, collaborations, and mentorship.

4624
07:19:16,910 --> 07:19:22,372
Building a network within the cybersecurity community can provide support and guidance throughout your career.

4625
07:19:22,766 --> 07:19:28,160
And many events also offer hands-on workshops and training sessions that can enhance your practical skills.

4626
07:19:28,320 --> 07:19:35,040
So by actively participating in these events, you can demonstrate your commitment to continuous learning and professional development.

4627
07:19:35,440 --> 07:19:40,452
Make it a habit to attend cybersecurity events regularly, to stay engaged and informed.

4628
07:19:40,750 --> 07:19:44,880
So this was all about number seven point that is not attending cybersecurity events.

4629
07:19:45,040 --> 07:19:49,440
Now moving to number eight, that is obsessing over which specialization to choose.

4630
07:19:49,678 --> 07:19:55,012
So when starting a career in cybersecurity, many beginners obsess over which specialization to choose.

4631
07:19:55,278 --> 07:19:57,764
This can be overwhelming and counterproductive.

4632
07:19:58,158 --> 07:20:04,708
Instead of stressing about making the perfect choice, allow yourself the freedom to explore different areas of cybersecurity.

4633
07:20:05,070 --> 07:20:11,492
The field is diverse, with specializations like penetration testing, incident response, security analysis, and more.

4634
07:20:11,822 --> 07:20:16,320
Take the time to experiment with various topics and see what interests you the most.

4635
07:20:16,590 --> 07:20:20,740
This exploration phase is valuable for gaining a broad understanding of this field.

4636
07:20:20,960 --> 07:20:26,756
So over time, you will naturally gravitate toward areas that align with your strengths and interests.

4637
07:20:26,990 --> 07:20:31,460
So remember, your specialization can evolve as you gain more experience and insights.

4638
07:20:31,950 --> 07:20:38,532
Early in your career, focus on building a solid foundation and gaining exposure to different aspects of cybersecurity.

4639
07:20:38,862 --> 07:20:47,920
This approach allows you to make an informed decision about your specialization when the time comes, ensuring you choose a path that truly excites and motivates you.

