6538
10:43:00,686 --> 10:43:04,164
The tester runs one or more scanner tools to gather more information about the target.

6539
10:43:04,878 --> 10:43:17,412
By using various scanners such as wall dialers, port scanners, network mappers, and vulnerability scanners, the penetration tester collects as many vulnerabilities which help in turn to attack a target in a more sophisticated manner.

6540
10:43:19,726 --> 10:43:27,364
In the gaining access phase, the penetration tester tries to establish a connection with the target and exploit the vulnerabilities found in the previous phase.

6541
10:43:28,110 --> 10:43:33,956
The exploitation may be a buffer overflow attack, denial of service attack, session hijacking, and many more.

6542
10:43:34,926 --> 10:43:41,252
Basically, the penetration tester extracts information and sensitive data from the servers by gaining access with different tools.

6543
10:43:42,286 --> 10:43:46,916
In the maintaining access phase, the penetration tester tries to create a backdoor for himself.

6544
10:43:47,534 --> 10:43:54,820
It helps him to identify hidden vulnerabilities in the system while allowing him to come back to the system to retrieve more data further on.

6545
10:43:57,006 --> 10:44:04,356
In the clearing tax phase, the tester tries to remove all logs and footprints which might help the administrator identify his presence.

6546
10:44:05,006 --> 10:44:10,052
This helps the tester to think like a hacker and perform corrective actions to mitigate those activities.

6547
10:44:11,150 --> 10:44:16,772
Nmap is most beneficial in the early stages of ethical hacking where a hacker must figure the possible entry point to a system.

6548
10:44:17,326 --> 10:44:25,124
