7621
12:49:58,542 --> 12:50:00,868
Welcome to this tutorial on penetration testing.

7622
12:50:01,358 --> 12:50:03,716
Let's go through some of the topics we will be covering today.

7623
12:50:06,638 --> 12:50:12,420
We start by learning about penetration testing and ethical hacking and the different use cases in the IT industry.

7624
12:50:13,646 --> 12:50:19,108
Next, we know about the benefits of penetration testing and how they help organizations save money in the long run.

7625
12:50:20,526 --> 12:50:28,068
Moving on, we familiarize ourselves with the different types of penetration testing or ethical hacking, with each serving a different category of personnel.

7626
12:50:29,358 --> 12:50:38,788
In the next section, we read about the five distinct phases in every ethical hacking campaign and how they help clear up the extensive report at the end of every penetration testing session.

7627
12:50:40,270 --> 12:50:49,392
Finally, we have a live demonstration on how we can check for vulnerabilities and the ways hackers can break into devices without adequate security measures in place.

7628
12:50:51,694 --> 12:50:54,692
Let's start by learning about penetration testing in general.

7629
12:50:57,550 --> 12:51:01,412
Organizations can define penetration testing based on the objectives of the test.

7630
12:51:02,030 --> 12:51:06,628
All networks, applications, devices, and physical security components are included.

7631
12:51:06,992 --> 12:51:10,436
It imitates the behavior of harmful individuals or the hackers.

7632
12:51:11,182 --> 12:51:19,940
Experienced cybersecurity specialists use penetration testing to strengthen a company's security posture and eliminate any weaknesses that leave it vulnerable to attacks.

7633
12:51:20,272 --> 12:51:26,756
Penetration testing, when done correctly, goes beyond simply preventing thieves from gaining unauthorized access to a company's systems.

7634
12:51:26,992 --> 12:51:34,820
It generates realistic scenarios that demonstrate how well a company's present defenses might perform in the face of a full-scale cyber assault.

7635
12:51:35,438 --> 12:51:40,868
The simulation aids in the discovery of the sites of exploitation and the testing of IT breach security.

7636
12:51:42,126 --> 12:51:49,252
Businesses may acquire professional, unbiased, third-party input on the security procedures by conducting frequent penetration testing.

7637
12:51:50,094 --> 12:51:56,484
Pen testing, while relatively time-consuming and costly, can aid in the prevention of highly destructive and expensive breaches.

7638
12:51:57,742 --> 12:52:03,556
A white hat hacker employs hacking talents to find security flaws in hardware, software, or networks.

7639
12:52:03,872 --> 12:52:09,712
On the other hand, white hat hackers follow the rule of law when it comes to hacking instead of black hat hackers.

7640
12:52:10,094 --> 12:52:16,324
They assist firms in conducting penetration tests to analyze their security index and make the necessary improvements.

7641
12:52:18,254 --> 12:52:27,140
Ethical hacking provides a full audit of your security policies and, in the case of bug bounties, can assist you in identifying holes in existing operational systems.

7642
12:52:27,392 --> 12:52:31,632
It takes a far broader approach to cybersecurity than penetration testing.

7643
12:52:32,142 --> 12:52:39,300
Whereas penetration testing focuses on system flaws, ethical hacking allows actors to utilize any attack tactics available to them.

7644
12:52:39,854 --> 12:52:51,232
They can take advantage of system misconfigurations, send phishing emails, launch brute force password assaults, breach physical boundaries, or do whatever else they feel will get them access to critical information.

7645
12:52:51,662 --> 12:53:02,724
Because thieves are progressively changing up the approaches and launching multi layered complex attacks, this is incredibly useful for determining just how exposed the organization is to cyber threats.

7646
12:53:04,206 --> 12:53:09,988
Considering the vast domain that is ethical hacking, we have multiple categories of penetration testing methodologies.

7647
12:53:10,382 --> 12:53:11,876
Let's cover them in the next section.

7648
12:53:13,070 --> 12:53:18,640
When configuring a security system, testing is critical to preventing hackers from penetrating the perimeter.

7649
12:53:19,022 --> 12:53:22,756
There are three sorts of tests: black box, gray box, and white box.

7650
12:53:23,918 --> 12:53:28,240
In the black box testing, the tester receives no information during the penetration test.

7651
12:53:28,400 --> 12:53:35,428
In this case, the pen tester takes the method of an unprivileged attacker from initial access and execution until exploitation.

7652
12:53:36,000 --> 12:53:42,880
This scenario is the most realistic, showcasing how an attacker with no inside knowledge may target and compromise an organization.

7653
12:53:43,310 --> 12:53:46,820
However, because of this, it is also the most expensive alternative.

7654
12:53:48,206 --> 12:53:57,444
White box penetration testing, which is also known as crystal box testing, entails sharing all network and system information with the tester, which includes network maps and passwords.

7655
12:53:57,934 --> 12:54:00,960
This saves time and lowers the overall cost of a project.

7656
12:54:01,390 --> 12:54:08,132
A white box penetration test effectively simulates a focused assault on a given system using as many attack paths as feasible.

7657
12:54:09,998 --> 12:54:16,580
In a gray box penetration test, also known as a transparent box test, very restricted information is present with the tester.

7658
12:54:17,198 --> 12:54:24,388
Gray box testing is beneficial for understanding the extent of access a privileged person may get and the possible damage they could wreck.

7659
12:54:25,102 --> 12:54:34,052
Greybox tests achieve a mix between depth and efficiency and may be used to mimic either an insider danger or an assault that has infiltrated the network perimeter.

7660
12:54:36,814 --> 12:54:44,740
Now that we covered the basics of penetration testing and the relative categories, one must know how these testing campaigns benefit the organizations conducting them.

7661
12:54:45,518 --> 12:54:48,068
Let us go through a few perks of penetration testing.

7662
12:54:51,278 --> 12:54:58,404
Regular penetration testing helps your business assess the security of online applications, internal networks, and external networks.

7663
12:54:58,702 --> 12:55:06,980
It also assists you in understanding what security measures are required to achieve the degree of protection your company needs to protect its people and assets.

7664
12:55:07,566 --> 12:55:13,924
Prioritizing these risks offer firms an advantage in anticipating hazards and preventing harmful assaults.

7665
12:55:14,798 --> 12:55:18,980
Penetration testing is similar to a real-life hacker rehearsing for a real-life hack.

7666
12:55:19,360 --> 12:55:25,764
Regular penetration testing helps you be proactive in your real-world approach to reviewing the security of your IT infrastructure.

7667
12:55:26,240 --> 12:55:32,324
The process identifies gaps in your security, allowing you to correct any flaws before an actual attack happens.

7668
12:55:34,990 --> 12:55:39,040
It is undeniably expensive to recover from the effects of a data breach.

7669
12:55:39,374 --> 12:55:46,720
Legal fees, IT cleanup, consumer protection programs, lost revenue, and dissatisfied customers may cost businesses millions.

7670
12:55:46,960 --> 12:55:57,188
Penetration testing regularly is a proactive strategy to remain on top of your security and may assist in preventing financial damage from a breach while safeguarding your brand and image.

7671
12:55:59,502 --> 12:56:10,532
Penetration testing aid in meeting the compliance and security duties imposed by industry standards and regulations such as PCI, HIPAA, FISMA, and ISO 27001.

7672
12:56:11,040 --> 12:56:20,900
Having these tests done regularly help demonstrate due care and your commitment to information security, all while avoiding the significant fines associated with the non-compliance.

7673
12:56:23,182 --> 12:56:28,292
With the entire process seeming to be a lengthy ordeal, what are the multiple phases in the process?

7674
12:56:28,640 --> 12:56:32,036
Theoretically, we have to follow a five-stage process.

7675
12:56:34,350 --> 12:56:37,316
Reconnaissance is the first phase of the penetration test.

7676
12:56:37,600 --> 12:56:41,572
In this phase, the security researcher collects information about the target.

7677
12:56:41,760 --> 12:56:48,400
It can be done actively, meaning you are collecting information by sending a request directly to the target and interpreting it.

7678
12:56:48,750 --> 12:56:53,360
Passively, where you are collecting data without contacting the target or both.

7679
12:56:53,838 --> 12:56:59,844
It helps security firms gather information about the target system, network components, active machines, etc.

7680
12:57:00,480 --> 12:57:06,116
This activity can be performed by using information available in the public domain and using different tools.

7681
12:57:08,462 --> 12:57:11,876
The scanning phase is more tool-oriented rather than performed manually.

7682
12:57:12,910 --> 12:57:17,380
The penetration tester runs one or more scanner tools to gather more information about the target.

7683
12:57:17,600 --> 12:57:30,052
By using scanners such as war dialers, port scanners, network mappers, and vulnerability scanners, the penetration tester collects as many vulnerabilities which help in turning to attack a target in a more sophisticated way.

7684
12:57:33,390 --> 12:57:35,972
The third phase is gaining access of the system.

7685
12:57:36,398 --> 12:57:43,076
In this phase, the penetration tester tries to connect with the target and exploit the vulnerabilities found in the previous stage.

7686
12:57:43,408 --> 12:57:49,508
The exploitation may be buffer overflow attacks, denial of service DOS attacks, session hijacking, and many more.

7687
12:57:50,446 --> 12:57:56,004
Pen tester extracts information and sensitive data from the servers by gaining access using different tools.

7688
12:57:58,158 --> 12:58:01,408
In the fourth stage, the hacker has to maintain access.

7689
12:58:01,838 --> 12:58:04,900
The penetration tester tries to create a backdoor from himself.

7690
12:58:05,358 --> 12:58:12,452
It helps the penetration tester to identify hidden vulnerabilities in the system and can later access the machine should the need arise.

7691
12:58:13,518 --> 12:58:22,340
In the final phase of clearing and covering tracks, the penetration tester removes all logs and footprints which help the administrator identify his presence.

7692
12:58:22,768 --> 12:58:28,772
This allows the penetration tester to think like a hacker and perform corrective actions to mitigate those activities.

7693
12:58:30,798 --> 12:58:37,808
With the cost of cybersecurity platforms going up, trained penetration testers receive an excellent level of remuneration for the efforts.

7694
12:58:37,998 --> 12:58:46,276
As per reports, the average yearly salary for a penetration tester is 6 lakh Indian rupees or $110,000 in the American counterpart.

