18:43:30,222 --> 18:43:33,616
Those are the newer mindsets of the threat hunter.

10918
18:43:33,696 --> 18:43:36,324
The threat hunter then learns how a business works.

10919
18:43:37,870 --> 18:43:39,856
and I can't emphasize that more.

10920
18:43:40,016 --> 18:43:43,776
You learn and you gain a clear understanding of the endpoints on the system.

10921
18:43:43,856 --> 18:43:50,176
That means all the IoT devices, all the phones, all of the IT, uh, all the desktops, et cetera.

10922
18:43:50,798 --> 18:43:53,696
You learn networking best practices that constitute a network.

10923
18:43:53,776 --> 18:43:57,616
So you then learn about how the network works, endpoints and also network infrastructure.

10924
18:43:57,776 --> 18:44:04,132
More importantly, you learn how information flows from one system in that network to another.

10925
18:44:04,462 --> 18:44:05,856
Because that's what hackers are doing to you.

10926
18:44:05,936 --> 18:44:07,696
And you find out what's going on.

10927
18:44:07,854 --> 18:44:22,256
So you're basically creating hypotheses and you're engaging in a kind of loop of thought, and then you look and you investigate network systems or endpoints to look for patterns and you look for indicators of compromise.

10928
18:44:22,478 --> 18:44:23,676
Some people call it TTPs.

10929
18:44:23,790 --> 18:44:25,696
I call it indicators of compromise.

10930
18:44:26,094 --> 18:44:32,964
And then you do some analytics and you start over again and you look through the infrastructure of your system, you look into the developers.

10931
18:44:33,358 --> 18:44:41,156
If you have a company that is focusing on code development, then you need to make sure how those code developers are working.

10932
18:44:41,486 --> 18:44:44,096
