10933
18:44:44,256 --> 18:44:58,976
So you as that information flows, and then as you focus on the technical elements that allow that information to flow and where it is stored, you then learn how that information can be interrupted and more importantly, manipulated.

10934
18:44:59,216 --> 18:45:04,096
Then you look for new network traffic, you look for new processes on the system, dropped files.

10935
18:45:04,176 --> 18:45:06,468
These are all examples of indicators of compromise.

10936
18:45:07,534 --> 18:45:12,704
Connections to strange places at strange times or strange places at normal times.

10937
18:45:13,424 --> 18:45:22,144
The threat hunter then reports these types of issues if he or she feels it's a problem to the security or secure operations center.

10938
18:45:22,304 --> 18:45:23,364
That's what a SOC is.

10939
18:45:23,790 --> 18:45:25,220
Secure Operations Center.

