11132
19:02:12,976 --> 19:02:16,416
As a threat hunter, you look for various types of compromise.

11133
19:02:16,576 --> 19:02:22,788
By intelligence, in other words, you go out and say, Well, we have these types of systems in our company that we think are the highest risk.

11134
19:02:23,216 --> 19:02:26,016
Let's say some WordPress uh sites.

11135
19:02:26,382 --> 19:02:30,016
So we can go out and do intelligence or behavior-based analytics.

11136
19:02:30,096 --> 19:02:30,896
They're both useful.

11137
19:02:31,056 --> 19:02:33,696
They're one's necess not necessarily better than the other.

11138
19:02:33,856 --> 19:02:37,796
Intelligence means, well, I've got a particular version of WordPress.

11139
19:02:39,982 --> 19:02:46,148
I'm going to go out and find out for that particular version of WordPress what the hackers are doing to it lately, what attacks are available.

11140
19:02:46,286 --> 19:02:47,296
That's a very useful thing.

11141
19:02:47,456 --> 19:02:54,500
But you can also look by behavior and see, well, who's logging on, who's not logging on, who uh what accounts are being used.

11142
19:02:54,656 --> 19:02:55,856
That's more behavior-based.

11143
19:02:55,936 --> 19:02:56,708
They're very useful.

11144
19:02:56,816 --> 19:02:59,524
And you then you ask yourself what the adversary is doing.

11145
19:02:59,854 --> 19:03:03,588
Well, is somebody conducting scans of the system reconnaissance?

11146
19:03:04,816 --> 19:03:06,788
are we in the middle of an initial compromise?

11147
19:03:07,086 --> 19:03:11,204
Are people moving from one system to the next laterally and taking over systems?

11148
19:03:11,376 --> 19:03:12,896
Are they stealing information?

11149
19:03:13,296 --> 19:03:15,616
The fancy phrase for that is data egress.

11150
19:03:15,886 --> 19:03:18,212
So there are two ways to go about doing this.

11151
19:03:18,926 --> 19:03:32,612
So with behavioral analytics, you can do network behavior analytics, kind of like what I was showing earlier, showing traffic anomalies or traffic patterns, and you can look at user behaviors, you know, how are specific users working, and you can model those.

11152
19:03:32,816 --> 19:03:43,136
Increasingly we'll see artificial intelligence help model data, uh uh user behavior, and then we can take that information and start making decisions.

11153
19:03:43,374 --> 19:03:45,696
And AI one day will start making decisions for us.

11154
19:03:46,096 --> 19:03:48,416
I don't think it'll replace our jobs necessarily.

11155
19:03:48,496 --> 19:03:53,604
I think it'll uh at least in the short term, it'll simply help us.

11156
19:03:54,208 --> 19:04:04,388
So moving along, the baseline that you will set up is where you do an inventory of various systems and devices in your network.

11157
19:04:04,928 --> 19:04:11,428
these devices are endpoints, are also network connectivity devices and of course the resources that you use.

11158
19:04:12,174 --> 19:04:16,356
And by resources I mean uh um let's see, yeah.

11159
19:04:16,688 --> 19:04:23,556
Uh uh basically you're using resources that are important to your system.

11160
19:04:23,822 --> 19:04:29,186
So you do a software inventory as well, not just a physical one, but layer seven is very important, the application.

11161
19:04:29,966 --> 19:04:33,728
And you configure you secure configurations, etc., and move on.

11162
19:04:33,808 --> 19:04:35,428
This is an example of baselining.

11163
19:04:35,662 --> 19:04:42,564
Then you look for outliers and you have to ask yourself, are those outliers, is that outlier important, or is it just you know something to ignore?

11164
19:04:43,568 --> 19:04:49,860
you have to figure that out yourself, and a threat hunter doesn't just ignore it or accept it, has to go in and investigate it.

11165
19:04:50,862 --> 19:04:53,088
So you engage in endpoint monitoring.

11166
19:04:53,488 --> 19:04:57,168
some of the problems with endpoint monitoring are uh something that's very controversial.

11167
19:04:57,248 --> 19:05:09,328
Some people think agents, well, they don't take up much room or much time, but there are a lot of times where security workers want to install agents for antivirus and agents for monitoring and agents for intrusion detection.

11168
19:05:09,518 --> 19:05:13,248
After a while, you've got so many agents they can conflict with each other, they can cause problems.

11169
19:05:13,328 --> 19:05:15,940
They can I don't know if they can slow systems down, it's happened.

11170
19:05:16,366 --> 19:05:20,448
But you have to basically sometimes they're dissolvable agents, by the way.

11171
19:05:20,528 --> 19:05:25,764
In other words, they work for a while, then they just kind of destroy themselves, and good guys and bad guys use these.

