It can also show connections of networks and that sort of thing.

11180
19:06:14,254 --> 19:06:20,804
So you can engage in hypothesis-based threat hunting as well as situational threat hunting.

11181
19:06:21,088 --> 19:06:27,204
Hypothesis meaning, well, let's see, we have a particular situation, I'm going to make an educated guess.

11182
19:06:27,488 --> 19:06:33,316
Situational is where you basically say, well, our company has recently purchased another company.

11183
19:06:33,728 --> 19:06:38,048
that other company has a lot of SCADA systems or a particular type of system.

11184
19:06:38,128 --> 19:06:40,928
Let's investigate that because that's a new element coming in.

11185
19:06:41,088 --> 19:06:43,748
We have a new situation, let's go take control of it.

11186
19:06:44,174 --> 19:06:45,248
Well, what happens next?

11187
19:06:45,408 --> 19:06:50,768
You make recommendations next to the security operations team, to the incident response team.

11188
19:06:50,928 --> 19:06:54,692
And remember, the incident response team is not necessarily just all techies.

11189
19:06:55,278 --> 19:07:01,668
That's going to be a PR person in there, legal, representatives of HR, certainly representative from the CEO or the board.

11190
19:07:02,288 --> 19:07:08,452
You'll be talking to the in a larger company, the chief security officer, always the CEO and the board.

11191
19:07:11,150 --> 19:07:20,928
one of the things I'll make a real quick applied example, was once talking to a person who was working on a conveyor belt controller system that was compromised by ransomware.

