22:24:00,752 --> 22:24:06,180
People think that these firewalls will analyze the contents of that packet, which is not correct.

13002
22:24:07,054 --> 22:24:20,132
When a definition for a packet filtering firewall says that these firewalls analyze packets, it means that they are only analyzing the source and destination IP addresses, port numbers, and the protocols that are mentioned in those packets.

13003
22:24:20,494 --> 22:24:26,052
These firewalls do not have the capability of deep packet inspection or a DPI as it is known.

13004
22:24:26,286 --> 22:24:35,172
If that capability comes into the picture, you're basically looking at an intrusion detection system or intrusion prevention system in today's world called as a next-gen firewall.

13005
22:24:35,694 --> 22:24:46,576
Okay, so a packet filtering firewall essentially will only analyze data packets for its source and destination IP addresses, port numbers, and the protocol that is being utilized.

13006
22:24:46,736 --> 22:24:56,004
It will then map that information to the rules that are there on the firewall, and based on those rules, it will either allow that a connection to happen or disallow that connection from happening.

13007
22:24:57,454 --> 22:24:59,620
The second type of is a proxy firewall.

13008
22:24:59,918 --> 22:25:03,136
These firewalls filter network traffic at the application level.

13009
22:25:03,278 --> 22:25:08,068
So when you say application level, they work at the layer 7 of the OSI model.

13010
22:25:08,366 --> 22:25:16,644
Packet filtering firewalls, since we have mentioned that they work on IP addressing and port numbers, will work on the network layer of the OSI model.

13011
22:25:16,816 --> 22:25:19,620
Also on the transport layer because you also look at protocols.

13012
22:25:20,142 --> 22:25:32,132
Proxy firewalls will work at layer 7, which is the application layer of the OSI model, and will deal with application level protocols such as HTTP, HTTPS, FTP, SMTP, and so on so forth.

13013
22:25:33,614 --> 22:25:37,056
And the third one is a stateful multi-layer inspection firewall.

13014
22:25:37,296 --> 22:25:40,896
These filter packets at the network, transport, and application layers.

13015
22:25:41,102 --> 22:25:45,988
So they basically do the job of the first and the second type of firewalls.

