23:01:42,830 --> 23:01:51,236
If there is any code that has already been written, this code will be reviewed manually and any flaws within that code would then be identified.

13325
23:01:51,598 --> 23:01:56,484
Static testing will always be 100% accurate in a very short amount of time because it is immediate.

13326
23:01:56,944 --> 23:02:01,412
You have created it, and then the export is going to test it to see whether everything is fine or not.

13327
23:02:01,824 --> 23:02:02,144
Right?

13328
23:02:02,304 --> 23:02:04,144
It is all about prevention mechanism.

13329
23:02:04,304 --> 23:02:09,344
So since you're doing it at the inception itself, if you find any flaw, it gets immediately repaired.

13330
23:02:09,424 --> 23:02:14,404
So this is about preventing vulnerabilities from keeping into that application at a later point in time.

13331
23:02:15,054 --> 23:02:19,104
Whereas dynamic on the other side is done at the end of the development lifecycle.

13332
23:02:19,246 --> 23:02:21,744
So you have generated the application, everything is ready.

13333
23:02:21,998 --> 23:02:23,492
Now you want to do dynamic testing.

13334
23:02:23,854 --> 23:02:26,052
Includes functional and non functional testing.

13335
23:02:26,286 --> 23:02:35,204
Functional testing is where the application itself is being tested, the functions to see that all the parameters that are given to the application are functioning properly.

13336
23:02:35,886 --> 23:02:41,700
Non-functional testing would be where security parameters, administrative parameters, all of them are being verified.

13337
23:02:42,350 --> 23:02:42,640
Right?

13338
23:02:43,086 --> 23:02:55,588
This is where your test case scenarios come in, and you're going to test each and every scenario by generating inputs and analyzing the output that the application is going to give you.

13339
23:02:56,462 --> 23:02:58,000
Dynamic testing is all about cure.

13340
23:02:58,080 --> 23:03:07,840
So here you're going to identify vulnerabilities, report them to the management, and the management is then going to figure out a way of patching those vulnerabilities so that they can be mitigated.

13341
23:03:08,110 --> 23:03:11,620
Moving on to the next question: what are the test levels in software testing?

13342
23:03:12,000 --> 23:03:20,772
So, as far as software testing is concerned, there are four test levels module testing, integration testing, system testing, and the final one is acceptance testing.

13343
23:03:21,166 --> 23:03:25,636
So, in the testing phase of your development lifecycle, the first thing is a module test.

13344
23:03:25,806 --> 23:03:32,320
you are going to check your routines, your subroutines, your subprograms, procedures that have been written in a program.

13345
23:03:32,462 --> 23:03:38,240
So all your functions, all your mechanisms for that application are going to be tested.

13346
23:03:38,478 --> 23:03:42,880
When you go into integration testing, the software may have been integrated with multiple softwares.

13347
23:03:42,960 --> 23:03:50,240
There may be different API calls coming in, maybe a third-party software on which you are depending upon to supply for information.

13348
23:03:50,446 --> 23:04:03,684
So all of these integration of various softwares, various APIs are tested to ensure that they are functioning properly and there are no flaws, errors, or mistakes left behind in the integration of all of these softwares.

13349
23:04:04,640 --> 23:04:11,120
Then the system testing is where the entire system, so including the hardware, including the software, right?

13350
23:04:11,310 --> 23:04:12,804
It starts from the installation.

13351
23:04:13,134 --> 23:04:14,788
So now the software is complete.

13352
23:04:14,990 --> 23:04:17,120
We know which hardware we are going to support for it.

13353
23:04:17,294 --> 23:04:24,644
We start by installing the software and see where the installation is going to be completed properly, if there are any errors in the installation process itself.

13354
23:04:25,614 --> 23:04:42,628
Then once it is installed, the performance of that particular application, the write speeds, the read speeds on the hard disk, the transaction speeds that the application is capable of, the network dependencies that the application may have, all of those would come under system testing.

13355
23:04:43,054 --> 23:04:52,452
And then the acceptance testing, which is basically a quality assurance exercise that the application meets the client's requirements.

13356
23:04:52,814 --> 23:04:56,740
So the client in the first stage would have given the scope of what needs to be achieved.

13357
23:04:57,134 --> 23:05:07,600
In the acceptance testing, you're verifying that that scope has been met and the client requirements have been met, and you can assure the client about the functionality and the performance of that particular application.

13358
23:05:07,854 --> 23:05:15,200
Coming to the last question in this software programs, what are the valuable steps to resolve issues while testing?

13359
23:05:15,360 --> 23:05:31,364
So, in the previous scenarios where we have started testing, now if you find out when you execute a particular use case and then you find out a flaw, what would be the steps that you would utilize to address those particular flaws in those tests?

13360
23:05:31,600 --> 23:05:38,372
The first step will always be record, then you're going to report it, and then you're going to introduce a control process for it.

13361
23:05:38,638 --> 23:05:45,600
So when you say record, you're going to create logs and you're going to try to resolve all the problems that have happened.

13362
23:05:45,710 --> 23:06:11,840
Now, when you say resolve, you're not going to recode the application, but you're going to test the system again and again to ensure that whatever is being recorded is accurate, and all the logs, all the error mechanisms, all the dumps, all of those that have been generated due to this particular log or, but due to this particular error are being captured so that they can be reported to the higher level managers.

13363
23:06:12,110 --> 23:06:26,400
So the next step is once you have re uh once you have accumulated all these logs and records, you're going to report them to the higher level managers who are then going to investigate it and go back to the developers trying to figure out the best way to mitigate those particular flaws.

13364
23:06:26,734 --> 23:06:34,240
So the report writing needs also also needs to be accurate, it needs to be to the point, it needs to detail what the problem was.

13365
23:06:34,400 --> 23:06:50,480
It will document all the steps that they were that you took, all the inputs that you put in, and it will also record all the errors, and it will also record all the mechanisms that were utilized and the uh errors that were generated.

13366
23:06:51,310 --> 23:07:00,784
And that report will be given to the higher level managers who can then forward it to the developers who, based on those reports, can try start their troubleshooting, and then the control mechanism comes in.

13367
23:07:00,944 --> 23:07:04,196
You're going to define the issue management process.

13368
23:07:04,622 --> 23:07:12,864
So this process needs to work in a particular manner where you're doing a test, you're recording whatever is happening, you're creating a report out of it, you're sending it to the management.

13369
23:07:13,070 --> 23:07:17,264
The management will then take those reports, study them, take it to the developers.

13370
23:07:17,344 --> 23:07:20,544
The developers will test based on their criteria.

13371
23:07:20,878 --> 23:07:40,452
They might interact with the testers at that point in time to identify particular flaws, and then they might want to recode that application on a developer patch, which, once installed, will mitigate that particular flaw, and then it can come back to the testing phase again, where you can repeat those tests and validate that the flaw is no longer existing.

13372
23:07:41,326 --> 23:07:46,884
So these are the three steps that would be utilized for testing purposes.

13373
23:07:47,822 --> 23:07:51,104
And that brings us to the first 10 questions on the software platform.

