13545
23:28:17,326 --> 23:28:28,624
The ZSH or the Z shell provides unique features like file generation, startup files, and fish friendly interactive shell, which provides features like auto suggestions and configuration.

13546
23:28:28,704 --> 23:28:34,308
So, all of these have different functionalities depending on what usage that you have for that particular shell.

13547
23:28:34,574 --> 23:28:41,424
The most common shell, like I stated, is the bash shell that you'll always come across in your desktop Linux operating systems.

13548
23:28:41,710 --> 23:28:44,864
Then looking at the next question, what are the process states in Linux?

13549
23:28:45,102 --> 23:28:45,984
Now, what is a process?

13550
23:28:46,224 --> 23:28:53,584
Process is basically a service that is running for a particular application for that application to function, right?

13551
23:28:54,144 --> 23:29:06,384
this process is going to direct user input to the processor, process it, get that output back to the application, execute it, and then show it onto the graphical user interface for the user.

13552
23:29:06,734 --> 23:29:09,824
So in Linux, there are five states for a process.

13553
23:29:10,094 --> 23:29:11,424
First is the ready space.

13554
23:29:11,726 --> 23:29:15,584
Now, in ready, in this state, the process is created and it is ready to run.

13555
23:29:15,664 --> 23:29:17,824
So it is waiting, uh it is waiting for input.

13556
23:29:17,904 --> 23:29:20,964
It's ready, the application is executed.

13557
23:29:21,646 --> 23:29:24,420
The running is when the process is being executed itself.

13558
23:29:24,782 --> 23:29:27,904
Blocked or wait is when user input is being looked upon.

13559
23:29:28,046 --> 23:29:31,844
So it's waiting for user input so that it can do the processing.

13560
23:29:32,366 --> 23:29:39,104
Completed or terminated, it has completed its execution or was terminated by the operating system for some reason or the other.

13561
23:29:39,310 --> 23:29:43,460
So this is when things have the processing has been completed.

13562
23:29:44,208 --> 23:29:50,928
And then last state is zombie where the process is terminated, but the process table still holds the information.

13563
23:29:51,488 --> 23:29:55,588
Maybe it is waiting for the kill request before it gets terminated.

13564
23:29:56,334 --> 23:30:00,128
So these are the five states for a Linux process to be in.

13565
23:30:00,398 --> 23:30:04,100
